1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Browser agents see the page now, but not what the organization learned yesterday.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
OrgMemory supplies durable, source-backed company context before action.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Without WebMCP: inspect the DOM, guess controls, navigate, and parse.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
With WebMCP: call a structured capability and receive authorized evidence.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The authenticated workspace preserves the signed-in person's access boundary.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
19 tools: 13 read-only and 6 human-governed.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
This is a real page-defined WebMCP invocation, not decorative playback.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Tool, arguments, results, and latency remain observable.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Payments is failing again. The agent asks for remembered incidents.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:10,000
It recovers pool exhaustion, checkout timeouts, and the surrounding service context.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Payments shares PostgreSQL with ledger, defining the blast radius.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:26,000
A prior decision capped worker concurrency to protect that shared pool.

13
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:35,000
OrgMemory turns precedent, dependencies, procedures, and decisions into action.

14
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Check connection count and the worker cap before improvising a new fix.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
The agent can propose verified knowledge, but nothing is saved yet.

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
A human reviews and decides. Capability is not authorization.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Approved knowledge becomes durable company memory, not another trapped chat.

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:16,000
That creates a clean handoff across agents, sessions, and tools.

19
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Session two is a brand-new agent: no shared chat, no carried context.

20
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:34,000
It still retrieves the procedure, incidents, service context, and prior decision.

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Read tools operate automatically inside the user's authorized scope.

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Writes remain proposals; approval remains a distinct human decision.

23
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
One governed company brain across every browser-agent session.

24
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Understand what happened before acting on what is happening now.
